// Plugin: no-raw-matchmedia
// Severity: error
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Catches:    A raw `globalThis.matchMedia(...)` / `window.matchMedia(...)` call
//             (or the bare structural-typed `.matchMedia` property access the DOM-less
//             `#lib` home casts through, e.g. `(globalThis as {...}).matchMedia`) —
//             ANYWHERE in packages/{client,ui}/src EXCEPT the two sanctioned lib
//             homes (`usePrefersReducedMotion` / `prefersReducedMotionNow`) and the
//             ONE legitimate non-reduced-motion viewport query
//             (`use-is-mobile-viewport.ts` — a DIFFERENT concern, the shell's single
//             `@media`/breakpoint site per UI-Architecture-and-Layout.md §4b axis 2).
//
// Rationale:  `matchMedia` forked raw in 4 primitives around the adjudicated one-home
//             hook (message-list.tsx/sortable.tsx called it in RENDER — doesn't
//             live-update on a mid-session media change; virtual-list.tsx/log-viewer.tsx
//             forked it inline in effects instead of importing the shared lib) — a
//             gate blind spot the DC4 rollup found (nothing stopped it). A raw fork
//             also drags a DOM-typed call into a DOM-less-typed graph (the sortable.tsx
//             TS7017 pair) the moment ANY consumer deep-imports past the barrel.
//
//               ❌ globalThis.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)")
//               ✅ usePrefersReducedMotion()        (render / live-updating)
//               ✅ prefersReducedMotionNow()        (imperative / point-in-time)
//
// Scope:      packages/{client,ui}/src, EXEMPT: the two lib homes themselves
//             (`use-prefers-reduced-motion.ts` / `reduced-motion-now.ts` — the ONE
//             place each is allowed to touch the raw global) and
//             `use-is-mobile-viewport.ts` (a viewport-breakpoint query, not reduced-
//             motion — its own one-home already, UI-Arch §4b axis 2).
//
// Refs:       docs/architecture/core/UI-Gates-and-Lessons.md §11 (matchMedia one-home)
//             packages/ui/src/lib/use-prefers-reduced-motion.ts
//             packages/ui/src/lib/reduced-motion-now.ts
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// GritQL note: two snippet arms cover both call shapes seen in the wild — the plain
// `$obj.matchMedia($args)` call AND the optional-chained `$obj.matchMedia?.($args)`
// form (`settings-shell-surface.tsx` / `view-transition.ts` guard the possibly-absent
// global that way; `?.(` parses to a DIFFERENT call-expression shape a plain-call
// snippet does NOT match). Both bind regardless of what `$obj` is (`globalThis`,
// `window`, or a locally cast structural type like `(globalThis as {...})`), so a
// future raw fork can't dodge the pattern with its own local structural cast.
// The three exempt files are the two lib homes (which legitimately hold this exact
// call) plus the one legitimate non-reduced-motion viewport-query file.

language js

or {
  `$obj.matchMedia($args)`,
  `$obj.matchMedia?.($args)`
} as $call where {
  $filename <: r".*/packages/(?:client|ui)/src/.*",
  $filename <: not or {
    r".*/packages/ui/src/lib/use-prefers-reduced-motion\.ts",
    r".*/packages/ui/src/lib/reduced-motion-now\.ts",
    r".*/use-is-mobile-viewport\.ts"
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$call, message="raw matchMedia call outside the one-home reduced-motion lib — use `usePrefersReducedMotion()` (render, live-updating) or `prefersReducedMotionNow()` (imperative, point-in-time) from `@orb/ui`'s `#lib` instead of forking matchMedia plumbing. See docs/architecture/core/UI-Gates-and-Lessons.md §11.")
}
